# Before the gate. dev-setup.sh runs in every verify job, as root in the Ubuntu container, and outside CI the cloud environment's setup script runs it as root at the start of every agent session (README.md). It decides which Node.js and browser builds CI downloads: the Node.js version of its NODE_VERSION, which must equal .nvmrc, and the browser builds that the @playwright/test version of package.json names, refusing any build without a SHA-256 in its BROWSER_PINS; it checks each download against the SHA-256 written in it before it installs it. pnpm is not pinned there: package.json's packageManager names pnpm's version, pnpm-lock.yaml records the SHA-512 of its native binary for each platform, and dev-setup.sh installs that binary only after pnpm-binary.ts has checked the download against it; then it runs `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`. ubuntu-packages.sh fetches the Ubuntu package files of deps/ubuntu-packages.lock, checks each against the lock and installs them with dpkg, which runs the packages' maintainer scripts as root in the container; its lock command is also the check that ties the lock to Ubuntu's signature, which the workflow "Ubuntu packages" runs again and compares with the committed lock. In the engine job, engine-package.sh builds the engine's WebAssembly package from the commit of bayan-core.pin with bayan-core's own setup script, after check-engine-pin.sh has refused any commit that is not on bayan-core's main branch, or that reached it less than 24 hours before now or before the commit that pinned it.
